course: dictionary
lesson: 757
title: BC, bc and other short words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: BC is written after a year. It stands for Before Christ, and it means that many years before the year 1 in the usual calendar. «Julius Caesar died in 44 BC.» The years count backwards, so 500 BC is earlier than 400 BC.
explain: BC can also be a place. «Brayden's mom lives in BC (British Columbia, the province next door).» Here there is no year, so it cannot mean Before Christ. British Columbia is a province on the west coast of Canada.
explain: In a text message, «bc» is a short way of writing «because». It is informal, so you will not see it in schoolwork. When you meet a short word like this, read the words around it and ask: which meaning fits here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: BC means Before Christ when it follows a year, such as «44 BC».
fact: Years BC count backwards: «500 BC» is earlier than «400 BC».
fact: There is no year 0, so «10 BC» and «AD 10» are 19 years apart, not 20.
fact: «BC» can also mean British Columbia, a province of Canada whose capital is Victoria.
fact: «bc» in a text message means «because», but never use it in schoolwork.
exercise: «Cleopatra died in 30 BC.» In this sentence, what does BC mean? | A town near a river | Because | *A year, counted as that many years before the year 1 | A province in Canada
exercise: «Brayden's mom lives in BC, the province next door.» What does BC stand for here? | Before Christ | *British Columbia | Big City | Because
exercise: A friend texts, «Cant come bc Im busy.» What does bc mean? | British Columbia | Before Christ | *Because | Black cat
test: Which year came first, «500 BC» or «400 BC»? | 400 BC | Neither, because BC years do not count | *500 BC | They are the same year
test: How many years are there between «10 BC» and «AD 10», given there is no year 0? | *19 | 9 | 10 | 20
exam: «There is no year 0, so a Roman born in 20 BC turned 39 on his birthday in AD 20.» How old was he in AD 20? | 41 | 38 | *39 | 40
